{
  "_comment": "Dark room, spinning two-blade fan under an overhead light. All three light types are authored (directional, spot, point), positioned to illuminate the fan, but only one is enabled by default -- switch via each light's Enabled checkbox in the debug UI to compare how directional/spot/point shadows look under motion. Spot is the default because it's the one that reads as 'a light above the fan' -- a bounded pool of light on the floor with the rest of the room dark -- unlike directional, which lights the whole floor evenly regardless of distance from the fan. Point-light shadow casting (B.15, cube-map on BSM/SV/PPS) is live, so all three light types can cast the fan's spinning shadow depending on active algorithm/mode support. render.fogAffectsSky (true here) makes the always-on procedural sky gradient fade to black past render.fogFar, on top of the room's own black IBL/ambient -- without it the horizon gradient would still show through even in a scene with zero ambient light.",
